-- An import cycle, reached indirectly.
--
-- A module is interned before its declarations are resolved, so a module reached a second time
-- while it is still being resolved exists and holds only what came before the import that led back
-- to it. Nothing downstream can tell that apart from a finished module, which is what made this
-- silent: the program still compiled, and what it meant depended on which file was named first.
--
-- Ring imports Loop and Loop imports Ring, so the cycle is closed one module below this one - a
-- direct self-import was already rejected, and this is the case that was not.

import Ring

fn main() -> Int = ringSize()
